cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "cubesphere: a high-order cubed-sphere spectral element transport solver in Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Chin-Kai"
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Funtrollor/cubesphere"
keywords:
  - cubed sphere
  - spectral element method
  - summation-by-parts
  - advection
  - Rust
  - GPU
abstract: >-
  cubesphere solves the transport (advection) equation on the sphere with
  Legendre–Gauss–Lobatto spectral elements on an equiangular or equidistant
  cubed-sphere grid. It uses a split-form divergence with conservative SBP-SAT
  interface coupling (upwind, central or blended flux) and low-storage
  Carpenter–Kennedy RK45 time stepping, and runs on a Rayon CPU backend or an
  experimental cuda-oxide GPU backend.
